.TH TRICKSTERCTL 1 "0.1.0" "trickster 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tricksterctl \- control client for a running trickster bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tricksterctl
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tricksterctl
is a short-lived client against the control socket of a running
.BR trickster (1)
bar. Each invocation sends one JSON request and prints one reply. It never
hosts a second engine or UI runtime.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the running state, outputs, and module states as JSON. This is the
default when no command is given.
.TP
.B version
Print the bar and control protocol versions.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read the configs now, the same path the file watcher uses. Prints
.B ok
or the parse error while the bar keeps its last-good state.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print the client version and exit.
.SH SOCKET
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/trickster/control.sock
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trickster (1)
.SH LICENSE
GPL-3.0-or-later.
